# Tab5 Source Rules

## Boot order (conceptual)

1. P4 hardware + IO expander (PI4IOE5V6408) — `WLAN_PWR_EN`, resets
2. Display (MIPI-DSI LDO + ST7123/ILI9881C) via M5Unified/BSP
3. **ESP-Hosted** SDIO link to C6 — transport up before any Wi-Fi
4. Application networking (`esp_netif`, HTTP, MQTT)
5. Camera/audio/IMU subsystems after power rails stable

## Arduino / M5Unified

```cpp
#include <M5Unified.h>
#include <WiFi.h>

#define TAB5_SDIO_CLK  GPIO_NUM_12
#define TAB5_SDIO_CMD  GPIO_NUM_13
#define TAB5_SDIO_D0   GPIO_NUM_11
#define TAB5_SDIO_D1   GPIO_NUM_10
#define TAB5_SDIO_D2   GPIO_NUM_9
#define TAB5_SDIO_D3   GPIO_NUM_8
#define TAB5_SDIO_RST  GPIO_NUM_15

void setup() {
    M5.begin();  // display, touch, expander, power
    WiFi.setPins(TAB5_SDIO_CLK, TAB5_SDIO_CMD, TAB5_SDIO_D0,
                 TAB5_SDIO_D1, TAB5_SDIO_D2, TAB5_SDIO_D3, TAB5_SDIO_RST);
    // now WiFi.mode / WiFi.begin
}
```

## ESP-IDF

- Dependencies: `espressif/esp_hosted`, `espressif/esp_wifi_remote`, `espressif/m5stack_tab5`
- Configure Tab5 SDIO2 GPIOs in hosted menuconfig (not P4-EV defaults)
- C6 ships with hosted slave FW; reflash slave only when updating co-processor

## Shutdown

Implement graceful shutdown: flush storage, disable radios, notify user, then trigger `PWROFF` via expander — do not yank power.
